# API service

- Follow existing FastAPI and Pydantic patterns; keep route handlers thin and modules simple.
- Place public endpoints under `/api/v1` and preserve established request, response, and status-code contracts.
- Validate all boundary inputs and outputs with explicit Pydantic models.
- Return stable, actionable errors with appropriate HTTP status codes; never leak stack traces, credentials, or internal provider details.
- Add only endpoints required by the current product scope. Do not create speculative CRUD, admin, auth, or integration endpoints.
- Keep backend product rules, knowledge access, provider calls, and validation in backend-owned modules.
- Do not modify frontend files while implementing API-only work; coordinate contract changes instead of silently breaking consumers.
